    "#5f7a8a"
   ]
  },
  "text": "Let us start in a laboratory. Pathologists once studied the brains of people who died of kuru. Under the microscope, the tissue was full of tiny holes.",
  "dur": 8.53,
  "transition_in": "page",
  "prev": "",
  "nxt": "Nerve cells had died, and what remained looked like a sponge. Doctors now call this pattern spongiform change.",
  "frog_hint": false
 },
