  "text": "In 1959, the researcher William Hadlow noticed that it looked a lot like scrapie, a disease of sheep.",
  "dur": 6.46,
  "transition_in": "zoom",
  "prev": "",
  "nxt": "Soon, experiments showed that the disease could be passed from one animal to another. So it was infectious. But something was off.",
  "frog_hint": false
