  "text": "In the early 1980s, the neurologist Stanley Prusiner suggested a radical idea. Maybe the agent was made of protein alone, with no genes of its own. He called it a prion.",
  "dur": 9.43,
  "transition_in": "zoom",
  "prev": "",
  "nxt": "Many scientists doubted him. But the evidence grew, and in 1997 he received the Nobel Prize.",
  "frog_hint": false
